course: dictionary
lesson: 5876
title: A word with a story
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A manger is a long, open box or trough that horses and cattle eat from. It holds hay or other feed. The context helps you: «the baby was laid in a manger, an animal feeding trough», where the words after the comma explain what a manger is.
explain: In the Christmas story, the manger is where Mary laid the baby Jesus, because there was no room at the inn. The manger is why people sing «Away in a Manger» at Christmas, and it stands for Jesus being born in a humble place.
explain: Words can also appear in phrases. «Dog in the manger» means someone who will not let others have something they cannot use themselves. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: does it still make sense?
fact: A manger is a long, open box or trough that animals eat from.
fact: «Manger» is the feeding trough where baby Jesus was laid in the Christmas story, because there was no room at the inn.
fact: In French, manger means "to eat", so «la salle à manger» is the dining room.
fact: «Dog in the manger» means someone who will not let others have what they cannot use themselves.
exercise: «Jesus was laid in a manger, which is an animal feeding trough.» What is a manger? | A bag for carrying hay | *A long open box that animals eat from | A high wooden fence | A small room for guests
exercise: In the Christmas story, why was the baby laid in a manger? | Because the king ordered it | Because it was raining | Because he was hungry and wanted to eat | *Because there was no room at the inn
exercise: «La salle à manger» is a French phrase. What does manger mean in French? | To walk | To sing | To sleep | *To eat
test: Which phrase means someone who will not let others have what they cannot use themselves? | Horse in the field | *Dog in the manger | Cat on the mat | Bird in the tree
test: «The horses munched hay from the manger.» What does manger suggest? | A wooden swing | A soft bed | A stable door | *A feeding trough
exam: Which is the best meaning of manger in a nativity play? | *A feeding trough where baby Jesus was laid | A tall tower | A grand palace room | A type of carol
